def are_collinear(p1, p2, p3):
    def slope(p, q):
        dx = q[0] - p[0]
        dy = q[1] - p[1]
        return dy / dx if dx != 0 else float('inf')
    return slope(p1, p2) == slope(p1, p3)
```

The function checks whether the three points lie on a single straight line by comparing slopes. It uses a nested helper that takes two points and returns the slope of the line joining them, using float('inf') for vertical lines to avoid division by zero. The main body then returns whether the slope from p1 to p2 equals the slope from p1 to p3. When two or more points coincide, the slopes default to the same value, which matches the expected result.

