A rectangle is inside another rectangle, with boundary contact allowed, when every corner of the inner rectangle lies on or inside the outer rectangle. For the lower left corner, x1 of the inner must be at least x1 of the outer and y1 at least y1 of the outer, and for the upper right corner, x2 of the inner must be at most x2 of the outer and y2 at most y2 of the outer. The function returns True when both lower bounds are satisfied and both upper bounds are satisfied.

