The function compares every cell at position (r, c) with its counterpart at row distance from the bottom and column distance from the right.

For an empty grid the answer is True by definition. Otherwise, for each of the first half of the cells, the variable row gives the distance above the bottom row and the variable column the distance to the right of the last column; those give the row and column of the cell this one coincides with under an 180-degree rotation. When the cell contents differ, the function returns False; when the entire grid is checked in this way and no mismatch is found, it returns True. The comparison goes only half way through the rows, so it pairs off each cell with its mirror image exactly once.

