        elif command[0] == "redo":
            if redo:
                document.append(redo.pop())
    return document
```

The document starts empty, and a redo history starts empty. Each command modifies these:

- A do command adds the value to the end of the document and clears the redo history, discarding any undone values that had been saved there.
- An undo command, when the document is not empty, removes the last value from the document and pushes it onto the redo history.
- A redo command, when the redo history is not empty, takes the most recently undone value and appends it back to the document.

When all commands are processed, the function returns the contents of the document, in order.

