Each command is handled in sequence. A 'do' command appends a value to the document and clears the redo list, so the undo/redo relationship ends at every 'do'. An 'undo' removes the last value from the document, putting it at the front of the redo list. The 'redo' command returns the oldest undone value, appending it to the document and popping the front of the redo list. Since all undos, redos and document contents are tracked per function call, the calls inside a single document are time-ordered exactly as the spec requires, and no history beyond the redo list is stored.

